<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day t-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day t-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 8.921 percent at Wednesday's auction from 8.958 percent at the previous auction on June 18.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 1.1 billion pounds and accepted bids for 1,248.000 million. Bills worth 665.300 million pounds mature on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Central Bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Sept 25, 1997 (Sept 18, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.921 percent (8.958)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 1,248.000 million (1,330.525 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,661.425 million (1,705.525 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.600 - 8.951 percent (8.600 - 9.023)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.600 - 10.002 percent (8.600 - 10.099)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 51 (88)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 91 (92)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
